# .dockerignore
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in the dockerfile pulls in secrets, personal
# data, and the host's own virtualenv. Two concrete failure modes this
# prevents:
#   1. Baking .env/.env.docker, memory.db, chroma_db/, and received_notes/
#      into the image itself — anyone who gets the built image gets the
#      real API_TOKEN/SMTP/Nextcloud/Gotify secrets plus the owner's
#      actual conversation history and voice recordings.
#   2. `COPY . .` runs *after* `uv sync` already built the correct venv
#      for the container's platform — copying the host's own .venv on
#      top of it can silently replace native-extension packages
#      (chromadb, faster-whisper, piper-tts) with host-arch binaries.
#
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore's custom rules at the bottom — same
# reasoning applies to what shouldn't leave the host either way.

.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

.env
.env.docker

data/
memory.db
memory.db-shm
memory.db-wal
chroma_db/
received_notes/

.vscode/
.claude/
